{% comment %}
  sections/testimonials-showcase.liquid

  A column of proof beside lanes of video reviews that never stop moving, and
  the modal one of them opens.

  ## It is a new section, not a mode of `sections/testimonials.liquid`

  That section is a row of written reviews against a filled panel, driven by
  `<carousel-slider>`, and every one of its settings styles that. This one is a
  wall of faces on a loop with no arrows, no slides and no pagination — the two
  share a subject and nothing else. Folding it in would have meant a Layout
  select whose two options had almost no settings in common, and a merchant
  scrolling past forty controls that do nothing in the mode they picked.

  So nothing in `sections/testimonials.liquid`, `blocks/_testimonial-*.liquid`
  or `assets/testimonial-product.js` is touched by this file. The private blocks
  here are `_showcase-*` and the component is `<testimonial-showcase>`; the two
  sections can sit on the same page without meeting.

  ## The surface is the theme's, setting id for setting id

  Colour scheme, background media, the four border widths, the opacity slider,
  the eight corner radii, the margins, the container, the animation family —
  every id here is the one `sections/feature-cards.liquid` and
  `sections/testimonials.liquid` already carry, and all three reach them through
  `snippets/spacing.liquid`, `snippets/background-media.liquid` and
  `snippets/container.liquid` rather than reimplementing them. A merchant who
  has set up either of those sections has set up this one.

  ## Two columns, and the lanes own the second

  Above 990px the copy sits beside the lanes; below it, above them. The intro is
  a fixed column and the lanes take what is left, because the lanes are the part
  that can absorb any width — a card is a ratio — and a column of text that
  grows to 700px is a column nobody finishes reading.

  `--sv-intro-width` is published by the intro block and read by the grid here,
  exactly as `--tc-intro-width` works in `sections/testimonials.liquid`: the
  block owns its box, the section owns where the box sits. At 0 the intro takes
  an equal share instead, which is what a section with one lane wants.

  ## The lanes are blocks

  One `_showcase-column` per lane, each with its own direction, speed, offset
  and list of reviews. `blocks/_showcase-column.liquid` documents why that is a
  block rather than a **Columns** number, and the short version is that a
  merchant can answer "why is that one going the wrong way" about a setting and
  cannot about an index.

  Speed, direction and pause-on-hover are the three controls this section was
  asked for, and they land in two places on purpose: the first two belong to a
  lane, because two lanes travelling the same way at the same speed is the one
  arrangement the design does not want; the last is the section's, because a
  customer's pointer does not know which lane it is over.

  ## Nothing is fetched for a video nobody opens

  Every card carries its poster and a `<template>`, and the modal is one element
  for the whole section rather than one per review — see
  `snippets/showcase-video-modal.liquid` and
  `assets/testimonial-showcase.js` for both halves of that.

  ## The modal lives outside the container

  It is rendered after the section's own markup rather than inside it. A
  `<dialog>` in the browser's top layer is not affected by an ancestor's
  `overflow`, `transform` or `filter` — but the theme editor's section wrapper
  and the background media's clip are both ancestors that would otherwise
  contain it during the entrance animation, before it is promoted.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    ---- the surface, from `sections/feature-cards.liquid` ----
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    Opacity goes into the colour rather than onto the element: `opacity` on the
    section would fade the cards along with the frame.

    With no colour picked the border is `currentColor`, which the colour filters
    cannot take an alpha channel from — there is nothing to read until the
    scheme resolves in the browser. `color-mix` does the same fade at that point
    instead, so both paths honour the slider.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'

  assign bw_top = 0
  assign bw_right = 0
  assign bw_bottom = 0
  assign bw_left = 0
  assign border_any = 0
  assign border_paint = ''

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign bw_top = s.border_width_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_right = s.border_width_right | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_bottom = s.border_width_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_left = s.border_width_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign border_any = bw_top | plus: bw_right | plus: bw_bottom | plus: bw_left

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ---- corners ----

    Four corners, twice — one set per device, behind the same Desktop/Mobile
    switch the padding and the gaps already use. Same defaults and the same
    reasoning as `sections/testimonials.liquid`: a section is a band that lifts
    away from what is above it and sits flush on what is below, and 40px reads
    as a soft lift across 1400px and as a heavy scoop out of a 390px screen.

    They reach CSS as one `border-radius` shorthand, in the order that property
    takes — top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left.
  endcomment
  assign r_tl = s.border_radius_top_left | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign r_tr = s.border_radius_top_right | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign r_bl = s.border_radius_bottom_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign r_br = s.border_radius_bottom_right | default: 0 | plus: 0

  assign r_tl_m = s.border_radius_top_left_mobile | default: r_tl | plus: 0
  assign r_tr_m = s.border_radius_top_right_mobile | default: r_tr | plus: 0
  assign r_bl_m = s.border_radius_bottom_left_mobile | default: r_bl | plus: 0
  assign r_br_m = s.border_radius_bottom_right_mobile | default: r_br | plus: 0

  assign margin_top = s.margin_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_bottom = s.margin_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the two columns ----

    `plus: 0` rather than `default` alone on the mobile pair: 0 is a gap a
    merchant can legitimately want on a phone — the lanes flush under the copy —
    and `default` would replace it with half the desktop value every time.
  endcomment
  assign gap_x = s.gap_horizontal | default: 56 | plus: 0
  assign gap_y = s.gap_vertical | default: 40 | plus: 0

  assign gap_x_mobile = s.gap_horizontal_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.gap_horizontal_mobile == nil
    assign gap_x_mobile = 28
  endif
  assign gap_y_mobile = s.gap_vertical_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.gap_vertical_mobile == nil
    assign gap_y_mobile = 20
  endif

  assign lane_gap = s.lane_gap | default: 32 | plus: 0
  assign lane_gap_mobile = s.lane_gap_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.lane_gap_mobile == nil
    assign lane_gap_mobile = 16
  endif

  comment
    ---- the inner content box ----

    The section itself pads nothing by default, because the lanes are supposed
    to run off the top and bottom edges of the band — a card cut in half by the
    frame is what says the column carries on past it, and 80px of section
    padding turns that into a tidy row of whole cards floating in a box.

    So the inset the copy needs lives here instead, on the column the copy sits
    in. The lanes bleed; the words do not. A merchant who wants the old
    behaviour back raises **Section padding** and lowers this, and both controls
    are in the editor rather than one of them being a number in a stylesheet.

    Four sides behind the same Desktop/Mobile switch the rest of the section
    uses, and the `nil` test rather than `default` for the mobile four: 0 is an
    answer a merchant can mean on a phone, and `default` would overwrite it with
    the desktop value every time.
  endcomment
  assign content_pt = s.content_padding_top | default: 80 | plus: 0
  assign content_pb = s.content_padding_bottom | default: 80 | plus: 0
  assign content_pl = s.content_padding_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign content_pr = s.content_padding_right | default: 0 | plus: 0

  assign content_pt_mobile = s.content_padding_top_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.content_padding_top_mobile == nil
    assign content_pt_mobile = 48
  endif
  assign content_pb_mobile = s.content_padding_bottom_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.content_padding_bottom_mobile == nil
    assign content_pb_mobile = 48
  endif
  assign content_pl_mobile = s.content_padding_left_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.content_padding_left_mobile == nil
    assign content_pl_mobile = 0
  endif
  assign content_pr_mobile = s.content_padding_right_mobile | plus: 0
  if s.content_padding_right_mobile == nil
    assign content_pr_mobile = 0
  endif

  assign media_position = s.media_position | default: 'end'
  assign align_items = s.align_items | default: 'center'

  comment
    The intro's column, stated on the section rather than read back from the
    block.

    `sections/testimonials.liquid` reads `--tc-intro-width` off its panel and
    uses it in the grid above it, which is a custom property travelling *up* the
    tree — they inherit downwards only, so that expression has always resolved
    to its fallback. This one is the section's own number, set on the element
    that owns the grid, and the block keeps a width of its own for the case a
    merchant wants the copy narrower than the column it sits in.

    At 0 the column takes an equal share, which is what a section with one lane
    and a centred intro wants.
  endcomment
  assign intro_width = s.intro_width | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    `false == blank` is true in Liquid, so a blank check would read "off" as
    "not set" and turn these back on. `nil` is the only value that means the
    merchant has not answered yet.
  endcomment
  assign show_intro = s.show_intro
  if show_intro == nil
    assign show_intro = true
  endif

  assign show_stats = s.show_stats
  if show_stats == nil
    assign show_stats = true
  endif

  assign pause_on_hover = s.pause_on_hover
  if pause_on_hover == nil
    assign pause_on_hover = true
  endif

  assign modal_autoplay = s.modal_autoplay
  if modal_autoplay == nil
    assign modal_autoplay = false
  endif

  comment
    ---- the modal ----

    One id per section, so two of these on one page cannot open each other's
    videos. It is also what the cards' play buttons fall back to through
    `data-overlay-open` when the component has not upgraded yet.
  endcomment
  assign modal_id = 'showcase-video-' | append: section.id

  comment
    The accent the intro's score and the cards' stars fall back to, so the
    pieces stay in step with each other without either knowing about the other.
  endcomment
  assign accent = s.accent_color | default: ''

  assign lane_stagger = s.animation_stagger | default: 140 | plus: 0
-%}

{%- capture section_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', section: s, declarations: true -%}
  --sv-gap-x: {{ gap_x }}px;
  --sv-gap-y: {{ gap_y }}px;
  --sv-gap-x-mobile: {{ gap_x_mobile }}px;
  --sv-gap-y-mobile: {{ gap_y_mobile }}px;
  --sv-lanes-gap: {{ lane_gap }}px;
  --sv-lanes-gap-mobile: {{ lane_gap_mobile }}px;
  --sv-content-pt: {{ content_pt }}px;
  --sv-content-pb: {{ content_pb }}px;
  --sv-content-pl: {{ content_pl }}px;
  --sv-content-pr: {{ content_pr }}px;
  --sv-content-pt-mobile: {{ content_pt_mobile }}px;
  --sv-content-pb-mobile: {{ content_pb_mobile }}px;
  --sv-content-pl-mobile: {{ content_pl_mobile }}px;
  --sv-content-pr-mobile: {{ content_pr_mobile }}px;
  --sv-align: {{ align_items }};
  {%- if intro_width > 0 -%}
    --sv-intro-col: {{ intro_width }}px;
  {%- endif -%}
  --showcase-radius: {{ r_tl }}px {{ r_tr }}px {{ r_br }}px {{ r_bl }}px;
  --showcase-radius-mobile: {{ r_tl_m }}px {{ r_tr_m }}px {{ r_br_m }}px {{ r_bl_m }}px;
  --showcase-margin-block-start: {{ margin_top }}px;
  --showcase-margin-block-end: {{ margin_bottom }}px;
  {%- if border_any > 0 -%}
    --showcase-border-width: {{ bw_top }}px {{ bw_right }}px {{ bw_bottom }}px {{ bw_left }}px;
    --showcase-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --showcase-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if accent != '' -%}
    --sv-accent: {{ accent }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="testimonial-showcase color-scheme-container color-{{ s.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1' }}{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-section-spacing
  {%- if s.stack_layer != blank and s.stack_layer != 'default' %} data-section-layer="{{ s.stack_layer }}"{% endif %}
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  style="{{ section_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media', settings: s %}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="{% render 'container', width: s.container_width %}">
    <div class="showcase__layout showcase__layout--media-{{ media_position }}{% if show_intro or show_stats %} showcase__layout--split{% endif %}">
      {%- if show_intro or show_stats -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          `children: true` staggers the column's own parts — the score row, the
          heading, the copy, the buttons — so the section opens as one cascade
          rather than as a wall of text arriving at once.

          `kind: 'text'` because that is what this column is. The lanes opposite
          take the image family, where the presets move a panel rather than
          splitting it into words.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <motion-effect
          class="showcase__intro"
          {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', section: s, children: true %}
        >
          {%- if show_intro -%}
            {% content_for 'block', type: '_showcase-intro', id: 'showcase-intro' %}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if show_stats -%}
            {% content_for 'block', type: '_showcase-stats', id: 'showcase-stats' %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </motion-effect>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        One `<motion-effect>` around all the lanes with `data-target=".showcase-lane"`
        and a stagger, rather than an effect on each lane. A lane is a merchant
        block — `{% content_for 'blocks' %}` renders them all in one call and
        passes no index — so there is no `forloop.index0` to turn into a
        per-lane delay. Targeting rather than `data-children` is deliberate: the
        effect's child is the custom element, not the lanes inside it, and a
        selector still finds them where a child list would not.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <motion-effect
        class="showcase__media"
        {% render 'motion-attrs',
           kind: 'image',
           section: s,
           target: '.showcase-lane',
           stagger: lane_stagger %}
      >
        <testimonial-showcase
          class="showcase__lanes"
          data-modal="{{ modal_id }}"
          data-pause-on-hover="{{ pause_on_hover }}"
          data-modal-autoplay="{{ modal_autoplay }}"
        >
          {% content_for 'blocks' %}
        </testimonial-showcase>
      </motion-effect>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Outside the section root — see the note at the head of this file on why a
  dialog cannot be rendered inside an element that may clip or transform it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'showcase-video-modal', id: modal_id, settings: s %}

{%- comment -%}
  Every setting below is a control a merchant reaches in the editor, and the
  schema is one element's styling surface: splitting it to get under Theme
  Check's count of 40 would split the thing the settings style.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% # theme-check-disable ExcessiveSettingsCount %}
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_showcase-column"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.headers.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.paragraphs.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_position",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.media_position.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.media_position.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.media_position.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.media_position.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "end"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_intro",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.show_intro.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.show_intro.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_stats",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.show_stats.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.show_stats.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "align_items",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.align_items.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.align_items.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:shared.position.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:shared.position.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:shared.position.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "stretch", "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.align_items.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "intro_width",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.intro_width.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.intro_width.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 800,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gap_device",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "desktop", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.gap_horizontal.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.gap_horizontal.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 56,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.gap_vertical.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.gap_vertical.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 40,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "lane_gap",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.lane_gap.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.lane_gap.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 80,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 32,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal_mobile",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.gap_horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 120,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 28,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical_mobile",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.gap_vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 120,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "lane_gap_mobile",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.lane_gap.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 60,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.headers.scroll"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.paragraphs.scroll"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "pause_on_hover",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.pause_on_hover.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.pause_on_hover.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.headers.modal"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.paragraphs.modal"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "modal_autoplay",
      "label": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.modal_autoplay.label",
      "info": "t:sections.testimonials_showcase.settings.modal_autoplay.info",
      "default": false
    },
    {
